   string that stays English in every language, so this set is checked against the source tree by
   LocalizationTests rather than kept by hand.

   To add a language: copy this directory to <code>.lproj — de.lproj, fr.lproj — and translate only
   the value, on the right of each "=". Leave every key on the left exactly as it is: it is what the
   code looks the string up by, not something a user ever sees.

   Strings that take a count are in Localizable.stringsdict instead, because how many forms a count
   needs is a property of the language rather than of the sentence.

   The note above each entry says where the string appears and what it is for. Where it contains a
   key name like ⌃Esc, a symbol like ▸, or a file name like badges.json, leave that part as it is —
   macOS and the app spell those the same everywhere.
